   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicTopology/Singular/LocalHomology/Noncompact.lean",
   "fix": "Generalize it to any `f : R \u2192+* S` and make it a public instance `PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete T) (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{w} f)` under `TauCeti/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/`. Use that instance here.",
   "issue": "`preservesColimitsOfShape_restrictScalars_uliftInt` states that `ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{w}` preserves coproducts when the ring lives in an arbitrary universe. That holds for any ring hom and has nothing to do with manifolds, yet it is `private`. Mathlib's instance (via `restrictCoextendScalarsAdj`, ChangeOfRings.lean:658-675) only covers module universes `max u\u2082 w`, so this fills a real gap.",
